WEBVTT

00:39:58.446 --> 00:40:01.359
But you're sitting there
with what actually is, in some ways,

00:40:01.383 --> 00:40:04.447
quite a radical idea of
there's this magnetic idea at the center.

00:40:04.471 --> 00:40:07.109
So how should we think
about politics right now?

00:40:07.133 --> 00:40:11.282
Even something as basic
as the left-right spectrum

00:40:11.306 --> 00:40:13.479
seems to be shifting before our eyes.

00:40:13.503 --> 00:40:15.046
I thought I knew what that was,

00:40:15.070 --> 00:40:17.432
and I don't think I know
what it is now so much.

00:40:17.456 --> 00:40:21.751
How do you see things now,
and where do you hope they go?

00:40:21.775 --> 00:40:24.809
DB: Yeah. Somewhere in the book,
I mention a theory of change,

00:40:24.833 --> 00:40:27.582
which is "ratchet, hatchet,
pivot, ratchet."

00:40:27.606 --> 00:40:31.666
So, we face a common set of problems:
World War II, The Depression, whatever.